Z||000006||terryk||11-23-2001||12:51 PM||||Hey Smokin GT. Grass Valley? I'm over in Foresthill.<P>The ST's dropped my cars more than the Eibach's (2+ vs 1.5-2"). The Eibach's aren't progressive like some of their other springs, but the ride is low enough and still civil. The ST's were stiffer (and cheaper). I think the ST's get close to the limits of the camber adjustment in the front too.<P>I still have my white SE with the Eibach's. I think they are worth the difference. Go to <A HREF="http://www.eibach.com" TARGET=_blank>www.eibach.com</A>  and get the part number then search the web for that number. I've seen them as low as $219 for the set.<P>You won't be using a standard floor jack anymore either.<P>Unless you need the adjustability, don't do the coilovers. The cost is high just for the rears.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||The Aura||11-23-2001||01:41 PM||||I've had my St springs in for about two years and love them. the ride is bloody stiff but i'm willing to trade mere bumps and nudges for the way they handle.<P>------------------<BR>1986 GT 4spd&gt; Suspension Techniques Springs, Poly Bushings, Bosal Brospeed 4.5" Exhaust Tips, Cross Drilled Rotors||||reg||14
